PKI/Trust Infrastructure is a framework of digital certificates, keys, and security services used to establish a secure and trustworthy digital environment. It provides the cryptographic foundation for digital signatures, encryption, and certificate management across the health network.&#xD;
&#xD;
Its purpose is to ensure the authenticity and non-repudiation of digital health transactions and clinical documents. It allows participants to verify that a health record has not been tampered with and was issued by a legitimate and verified authority.&#xD;
&#xD;
Example: A certificate authority that issues digital "stamps" used by doctors to sign electronic prescriptions or laboratory results.
